[1m[38;5;231mWhen a task is deleted, what happens to its notification events?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mKeep them (recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mEvents survive via snapshot; "open task" is disabled. Honest history, and the unread badge never jumps for [39m
     [38;5;246munexplained reasons. Costs one branch in the render.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Cascade delete
     [38;5;246mDeleting a task removes its events. Simpler model, no orphan state — but the unread count can drop with no visible
[39m     [38;5;246mcause.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Delete unread, keep read
     [38;5;246mCompromise: silently drop pending noise, preserve history you already saw. More rules to explain than either pure [39m
     [38;5;246moption.[39m
